font-style: inherit;">=</span><span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"utf-8"</span>) <span class="im" style="color: #00769E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">as</span> f:</span>
<span id="cb4-3">        all_phrases <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> json.load(f)</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
<p>The <code>all_phr.json</code> file contains standardized echocardiogram report phrases organized by anatomical structures and clinical findings. It’s a comprehensive template library that maps cardiac assessment categories to their corresponding clinical descriptions.</p>
<pre class="{json}"><code>{
  "Anatomical Structure": {
    "Measurement/Finding Category": [
      "Phrase 1",
      "Phrase 2",
      ...
    ]
  }
}</code></pre>
<p>Opens file in JSON format and loads its content into the variable all_phrases</p>
<div id="df359e20" class="cell" data-execution_count="5">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb6" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb6-1">all_phrases</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
<div id="14df8e7f" class="cell" data-execution_count="6">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb7" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb7-1">t_list <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> {k: [all_phrases[k][j] <span class="cf" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">for</span> j <span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">in</span> all_phrases[k]] <span class="cf" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">for</span> k <span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">in</span> all_phrases}</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
<p>The line extracts phrase lists from the nested dictionary structure for each section.</p>
<p>For example, it extracts all the phrases related to <code>"Left Ventricle"</code> and stores them in <code>t_list</code> under the same key. For the key <code>"Left Ventricle"</code>, t_list will contain a list of all phrases associated with that section, such as <code>"Left ventricle not well visualized."</code>, <code>"Left ventricle is grossly normal in size and systolic function."</code>, <code>"Left ventricle is normal in size and systolic function."</code>, <code>"The left ventricle is small by linear cavity dimension."</code></p>
<div id="04d3bc95" class="cell" data-execution_count="7">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb8" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb8-1">phrases_per_section_list <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> {</span>
<span id="cb8-2">    k: functools.<span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">reduce</span>(<span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">lambda</span> a, b: a <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> b, v) <span class="cf" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">for</span> (k, v) <span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">in</span> t_list.items()</span>
<span id="cb8-3">}</span>
<span id="cb8-4"></span>
<span id="cb8-5">phrases_per_section_list_org <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> {</span>
<span id="cb8-6">    k: functools.<span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">reduce</span>(<span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">lambda</span> a, b: a <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> b, v) <span class="cf" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">for</span> (k, v) <span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">in</span> t_list.items()</span>
<span id="cb8-7">}</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
<p>The code flattens nested lists of phrases for each section into single lists using <code>functools.reduce</code>.</p>
<p>For example,</p>
<div id="f0b27424" class="cell" data-execution_count="8">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb9" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb9-1"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Before (t_list structure - nested lists)</span></span>
<span id="cb9-2"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Left Ventricle"</span>: [</span>
<span id="cb9-3">    [<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Left ventricle not well visualized."</span>],</span>
<span id="cb9-4">    [<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Normal LV size."</span>, <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Dilated LV."</span>],</span>
<span id="cb9-5">    [<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Normal wall thickness."</span>, <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Mild hypertrophy."</span>]</span>
<span id="cb9-6">]</span>
<span id="cb9-7"></span>
<span id="cb9-8"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># After (phrases_per_section_list - flat list)</span></span>
<span id="cb9-9"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Left Ventricle"</span>: [</span>
<span id="cb9-10">    <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Left ventricle not well visualized."</span>,</span>
<span id="cb9-11">    <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Normal LV size."</span>,</span>
<span id="cb9-12">    <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Dilated LV."</span>,</span>
<span id="cb9-13">    <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Normal wall thickness."</span>,</span>
<span id="cb9-14">    <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"Mild hypertrophy."</span></span>
<span id="cb9-15">]</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
<p>Summary: - The code initializes language-specific phrases for different sections by loading them from a JSON file. - It flattens nested lists of phrases into single lists for easier processing (<code>phrases_per_section_list</code> and <code>phrases_per_section_list_org</code>). - It converts these phrases into regex patterns to facilitate text matching later on (<code>regex_per_section</code>).</p>
<div id="6abcd5b4" class="cell" data-execution_count="9">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb10" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb10-1">device <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> torch.device(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"cuda"</span> <span class="cf" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">if</span> torch.cuda.is_available() <span class="cf" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">else</span> <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"cpu"</span>)</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
<p>Device agnostic code setup for PyTorch to use GPU if available, otherwise CPU.</p>
<div id="b467331d" class="cell" data-execution_count="10">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb11" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb11-1">checkpoint <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> torch.load(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"model_data/weights/echo_prime_encoder.pt"</span>, map_location<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span>device)</span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
<p>checkpoint is an OrderedDict from the collections module</p>
<div id="0736a240" class="cell" data-execution_count="11">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb12" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb12-1">echo_encoder <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> torchvision.models.video.mvit_v2_s() </span>
<span id="cb12-2">echo_encoder.head[<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span>] <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> torch.nn.Linear(echo_encoder.head[<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span>].in_features, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">512</span>)</span>
<span id="cb12-3">echo_encoder.load_state_dict(checkpoint)</span>
<span id="cb12-4">echo_encoder.<span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">eval</span>() <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Set the model in evaluation mode</span></span>
<span id="cb12-5">echo_encoder.to(device)</span>
<span id="cb12-6"><span class="cf" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">for</span> param <span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">in</span> echo_encoder.parameters():</span>
<span id="cb12-7">    param.requires_grad <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> <span class="va" style="color: #111111;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">False</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>
<p>Constructs a small MViTV2 architecture and loads the pre-trained weights from the checkpoint. The model is set to evaluation mode, moved to the appropriate device (CPU or GPU), and all parameters are frozen to prevent further training.</p>
<div id="5445e424" class="cell" data-execution_count="12">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb13" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb13-1">vc_state_dict <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> torch.load(<span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"model_data/weights/view_classifier.pt"</span>)</span>
<span id="cb13-2">view_classifier <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> torchvision.models.convnext_base()</span>
<span id="cb13-3">view_classifier.classifier[<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span>] <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> torch.nn.Linear(</span>
<span id="cb13-4">    view_classifier.classifier[<span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span>].in_features, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">11</span></span>
<span id="cb13-5">)</span>
<span id="cb13-6">view_classifier.load_state_dict(vc_state_dict)</span>
<span id="cb13-7"></span>
<span id="cb13-8">view_classifier.to(device)</span>
<span id="cb13-9">view_classifier.<span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">eval</span>()</span>
<span id="cb13-10"><span class="cf" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
font-weight: bold;
font-style: inherit;">for</span> param <span class="kw" style="color: #003B4F;
background-color: null;
